  "worked_solution": "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is $x=y=0,$ which gives the point $(0,0).$ So, I is true.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which gives a circle of radius $1.$ So, II is true.\n\n- If $c=4,$ the level curve is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16,$ which gives a circle of radius $4.$ So, III is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
